### Tested versions

Tested in 4.7-stable C# and GDScript

### System information

Windows 11

### Issue description

When using _**set_parallel(true)**_, tween callback is called immediately,
```C#
public partial class Bug : Sprite2D
{
    public override async void _Ready()
    {
        DateTime callbackTime = DateTime.UnixEpoch, finishedTime = DateTime.UnixEpoch;

        var tween = CreateTween().SetParallel(true);
        tween.TweenProperty(this, "rotation", 3, 4);
        tween.TweenProperty(this, "modulate", Colors.Red, 4);
        tween.TweenCallback(Callable.From(() => { callbackTime = DateTime.UtcNow; }));

        await ToSignal(tween, Tween.SignalName.Finished);
        finishedTime = DateTime.UtcNow;
        GD.Print(finishedTime - callbackTime);
    }
}
```
but works properly if _**parallel()**_  is used for the tween property instead:

```C#
public partial class Bug : Sprite2D
{
    public override async void _Ready()
    {
        DateTime callbackTime = DateTime.UnixEpoch, finishedTime = DateTime.UnixEpoch;

        var tween = CreateTween();
        tween.Parallel().TweenProperty(this, "rotation", 3, 4);
        tween.Parallel().TweenProperty(this, "modulate", Colors.Red, 4);
        tween.TweenCallback(Callable.From(() => { callbackTime = DateTime.UtcNow; }));

        await ToSignal(tween, Tween.SignalName.Finished);
        finishedTime = DateTime.UtcNow;
        GD.Print(finishedTime - callbackTime);
    }
}
```

### Steps to reproduce

Run the above C# code or MRP (in GDScript).

